T*
(1. Meaning and use) Tj
T*
(Currently means "at the present time" or "now". It is useful in neutral and formal English) Tj
T*
(when describing a situation in progress.) Tj
T*
(It is a false friend when Spanish corrientemente means normally, commonly, or ordinarily.) Tj
T*
(Choose the English word that matches the intended idea.) Tj
T*
(2. Bilingual examples) Tj
T*
(She is currently preparing for her Cambridge examination.) Tj
T*
(Actualmente se está preparando para su examen de Cambridge.) Tj
T*
(I normally work from home.) Tj
T*
(Normalmente trabajo desde casa.) Tj
T*
(This expression is commonly used.) Tj
T*
(Esta expresión se usa comúnmente.) Tj
T*
(3. Rules and common mistakes) Tj
T*
(Currently often appears before a main verb but after be: I currently work - Actualmente) Tj
T*
(trabajo; I am currently working - Actualmente estoy trabajando. It can also begin a) Tj
T*
(sentence.) Tj
T*
(Do not choose currently just because a Spanish sentence contains actualmente or) Tj
T*
(corrientemente; first decide whether the meaning is now, normally, or commonly.) Tj
T*
(Study tip: Read the English sentence aloud first, then check the Spanish meaning.) Tj
T*
(4. Practice) Tj
T*
(? Choose: I ___ take the train to work if you mean every day. \(currently / normally\)) Tj
T*
(? Translate: Actualmente estoy buscando trabajo.) Tj
T*
(Answers: normally · I am currently looking for work. - Actualmente estoy buscando trabajo. -) Tj
T*
(Actualmente estoy buscando trabajo.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
