T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Meaning and use) Tj
T*
(Direct speech repeats exact words in quotation marks. Reported speech communicates the) Tj
T*
(message without quoting every word.) Tj
T*
(With a past reporting verb, English often backshifts: present simple ? past simple; present) Tj
T*
(continuous ? past continuous; present perfect ? past perfect; past simple ? past perfect.) Tj
T*
(2. Bilingual examples) Tj
T*
("I am tired," she said. ? She said that she was tired.) Tj
T*
(«Estoy cansada», dijo. ? Dijo que estaba cansada.) Tj
T*
("I have finished." ? He said he had finished.) Tj
T*
(«He terminado». ? Dijo que había terminado.) Tj
T*
("I haven't submitted the report yet," he explained. ? He explained that he hadn't submitted) Tj
T*
(the report yet.) Tj
T*
(«Todavía no he entregado el informe», explicó. ? Explicó que todavía no lo había entregado.) Tj
T*
(3. Rules and common mistakes) Tj
T*
(Pronouns and time/place expressions may change with the new viewpoint: tomorrow can become) Tj
T*
(the next day, here can become there, and now can become then.) Tj
T*
(Backshift is not always compulsory when the information remains true. Meaning and context) Tj
T*
(matter more than mechanical transformation.) Tj
T*
(Study tip: Read the English sentence aloud first. Try to explain it before checking the) Tj
T*
(Spanish translation.) Tj
T*
(4. Practice) Tj
T*
(? Report: "I am leaving now," Ana said.) Tj
T*
(? Report: "I saw him yesterday," Luis said.) Tj
T*
(Answers: Ana said that she was leaving then. - Ana dijo que se iba entonces. · Luis said) Tj
T*
(that he had seen him the day before. - Luis dijo que lo había visto el día anterior.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
