(Learn English with TV Shows and Movies) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. A simple four-step method) Tj
T*
(? Watch for context. Notice who is speaking, where they are, and what is happening.) Tj
T*
(? Replay with English subtitles. Write down 3-5 useful expressions.) Tj
T*
(? Listen without reading. Try to recognize the expressions you studied.) Tj
T*
(? Imitate one sentence. Copy the rhythm and intonation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Realistic goal: learning one reusable phrase is more valuable than translating every word in) Tj
T*
(a long scene.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. What works well for beginners?) Tj
T*
(Choose shows with everyday conversations, short episodes, and clear visual situations such) Tj
T*
(as family life, friendships, school, work, restaurants, or travel.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. How to choose movies) Tj
T*
(Stories you already know, animation, and family movies can be easier because the context) Tj
T*
(lets you focus on the language. Avoid highly technical dialogue at first.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. How to use subtitles) Tj
T*
(Stage Subtitles Goal 1 Your strongest language Understand context 2 English Connect sound) Tj
T*
(and spelling 3 None Train listening) Tj
T*
(5. Phrases to listen for) Tj
T*
(? What's going on? - ¿Qué está pasando?) Tj
T*
(? Are you okay? - ¿Estás bien?) Tj
T*
(? I don't know. - No lo sé.) Tj
T*
(? Come on! - ¡Vamos!) Tj
T*
(? Wait a minute. - Espera un momento.) Tj
T*
(? What do you mean? - ¿Qué quieres decir?) Tj
T*
(? That's great! - ¡Eso es genial!) Tj
T*
(? See you later. - Hasta luego.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Weekly routine) Tj
T*
(Day Activity Monday Short scene + 5 expressions Tuesday Replay without subtitles Wednesday) Tj
T*
(Imitate 5 sentences aloud Thursday New scene + vocabulary Friday Review 10 expressions) Tj
T*
(Weekend Watch for enjoyment and notice what you recognize Keep learning Continue with) Tj
T*
(another lesson and keep practicing.) Tj
T*
(View all lessons ?) Tj
T*
