(1. Meaning and use) Tj
T*
(A negative prefix changes a word toward an opposite, negative, or incorrect meaning. English) Tj
T*
(uses several prefixes, so learning common patterns is more reliable than translating) Tj
T*
(directly from Spanish.) Tj
T*
(Un- is very common: happy ? unhappy; employed ? unemployed. In- often appears with Latin) Tj
T*
(roots: accurate ? inaccurate; dependent ? independent. Before m or p, in- commonly becomes) Tj
T*
(im-: possible ? impossible; patient ? impatient.) Tj
T*
(2. Bilingual examples) Tj
